WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.620
- It's time for my first guest everybody,

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.030
she is such a good person,

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.370
she'd probably rescue a
pig from a fire as well.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.670
She probably has.

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.240
She's an Emmy, Grammy and
Golden Globe nominated

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.960
actress, singer, and songwriter.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.950
She's killing it on This Is Us

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.900
and she's got two new
Christmas songs out now.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.264
I love Christmas, I
cannot wait to hear them,

00:00:16.264 --> 00:00:19.497
please welcome Mandy Moore, everybody.

00:00:19.497 --> 00:00:22.427
(audience cheering)
(smooth music)

00:00:22.427 --> 00:00:24.010
Hello, how are you?

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:27.660
- I'm well, how are you?

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.493
- I'm so good.

00:00:28.493 --> 00:00:29.560
You look, okay this is my thing,

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.690
I get so jealous of people
that can wear turtlenecks

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:32.940
'cause you look so great.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.240
I love people in turtle necks,

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.923
but I can't, I feel like
I'm being strangled all day.

00:00:36.923 --> 00:00:38.950
- I can't lie, I must have like,

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.770
you know, some Diane
Keaton in me or something,

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.152
I just, I love a turtleneck.

00:00:42.152 --> 00:00:43.085
(laughing)

00:00:43.085 --> 00:00:45.197
- That is a Diane Keaton
thing, that's amazing.

00:00:45.197 --> 00:00:47.660
Well we were just talking to a pig farmer,

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.080
so would you ever want a farm?

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.820
I feel like you would, you would be,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.430
you would fit in on a farm.

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:54.930
- That story just completely made my day.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.980
I was, I had to sort of stop myself

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:59.143
from getting too
emotional listening to it.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:02.080
To have a farm one day,
you know, it's funny,

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.900
I, I'm a big hiker and I
was hiking Everest base camp

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.400
that trek in Nepal last year

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.990
and the higher you get in the mountains,

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:13.570
you're sort of surrounded by yaks

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:17.040
because they're the main
source of transportation.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.180
And a lot of like the,

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:20.915
as, as you get like higher
and higher in the mountains,

00:01:20.915 --> 00:01:23.620
it's like their source of food as well.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:27.250
And so you have a lot
of like yak milk in tea

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.930
and you have yak cheese

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:31.730
and I just kind of fell in
love with the taste of, of,

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.240
of yak products.
- Yeah.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.333
- And I had it set in my mind,

00:01:34.333 --> 00:01:36.060
like I should open a yak farm,

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:37.430
I feel like there are no yak farms.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.300
You can't find yak products anywhere.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.690
- I was just thinking I've
never seen a yak or, yeah.

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:44.020
- They're beautiful

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.480
and obviously very strong,

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:49.011
but yeah, you, you have to
live in a very cold environment

00:01:49.011 --> 00:01:50.490
to, to have a yak.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.740
So those dreams were dashed for now,

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.960
but I don't know maybe, maybe
at some point later in life

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:55.990
I'll have a farm.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:57.840
- I'm amazed, I, we've toured together,

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.550
like we've been around
each other a little bit

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.470
and I, I, I mean, I felt
like I knew you a little bit

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:03.303
like who you are,

00:02:03.303 --> 00:02:04.940
but I don't think I had a clue

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:07.600
because you like, full-on skydive,

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:08.520
you don't hike,

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.940
you like you trek up mountains.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.330
Like you do things that people like,

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.510
those are like bucket list things

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.060
and you do them like
regularly, like you love it.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:18.230
I didn't know you were so adventurous.

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:20.490
- I feel like I've like come into this

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:23.235
slightly more adventurous streak
a little bit later in life.

00:02:23.235 --> 00:02:26.180
I've been skydiving several times,

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:29.980
but the trekking and the
climbing and hiking has,

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:31.820
has become a new found obsession for me.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:33.010
It's incredible,

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:35.160
but yeah, I--
- It seems therapeutic.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.250
- I look forward to, it's,

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.300
it's so cathartic, it's so therapeutic,

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:43.677
I can't wait to do more of
it once I pop this baby out.

